        "committerDate": "2026-10-03T22:15:04-05:00",
        "subject": "Draw an orb from a preview sheet in Firefox, where it was black. The loader cut each cube's faces out of the decoded sheet with createImageBitmap's rectangle; in Firefox such a bitmap reports the face's size, but WebGL uploads the whole sheet behind it, which the face's texture refuses, so every orb of the UMN tour was black on Firefox for Android, and on Firefox 157 on this Mac. The faces are now cut through a canvas, which gives each a bitmap of its own pixels. scripts/lib/headlessFirefox.mjs drives the installed Firefox headless over WebDriver BiDi with a profile in the run's folder, and scripts/lib/headlessPage.mjs gives a check one page, served by the check, that is the same in Chrome and Firefox; preview-sheet.mjs --browser=firefox uses it: the orb from the sheet was 6.5 to 9.2 dB from the orb from its files before, and is 50.6 to 51.0 dB on WebGL 2 and WebGL 1 now, as Chrome's three renderers still are. The validation guide says what Firefox does with such a bitmap, and the app files page that the live tour's worker installed, kept its 63 files and reloaded from them in Firefox."
      },
      "historyStatus": "Original revision preserved; reviewed six-commit isolated history attached to the destination migration branch",
      "extractedLastChangedRevision": "d742f26c878faa1c7459171f32ce8a1857cbbed4"
